content:
The syntax error was the use of an **undeclared register `q`** — the 8-bit shift register storage element was never declared inside `top_module`, so the simulator could not bind `q` or any of its bits (`q[0]`…`q[7]`).

**Fix:** declare `reg [7:0] q;` inside the module (and use blocking assignments plus a `default` in the combinational `case` to avoid inferring latches).

```verilog
module top_module (
	input clk,
	input enable,
	input S,
	input A,
	input B,
	input C,
	output reg Z
);

	// 8-bit shift register storage (Q[0]..Q[7]) -- this declaration was missing
	reg [7:0] q;

	// Shift register: S is shifted in first, synchronous active-high enable
	always @(posedge clk) begin
		if (enable) begin
			q <= {q[6:0], S};
		end
	end

	// 8:1 multiplexer: ABC selects which flop output drives Z
	always @(*) begin
		case ({A, B, C})
			3'b000: Z = q[0];
			3'b001: Z = q[1];
			3'b010: Z = q[2];
			3'b011: Z = q[3];
			3'b100: Z = q[4];
			3'b101: Z = q[5];
			3'b110: Z = q[6];
			3'b111: Z = q[7];
			default: Z = 1'b0;
		endcase
	end

endmodule
```
